<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pequot War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1636">1636</a>–<a href="/years/1638">1638</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pequot War was fought from 1636 to 1638 in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a> between the Pequot people and the colonies of Massachusetts Bay, Plymouth and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a>, with their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narragansett-people">Narragansett</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohegan">Mohegan</a> allies. Its central event was the Mystic massacre of May 1637, in which colonists burned a fortified Pequot village; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-hartford-1638">Treaty of Hartford (1638)</a> dissolved the Pequot as a nation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pequot-war.jpg" alt="Pequot War" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pequot_war.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
